{
  "id": "surface-dyslexia",
  "term": "surface dyslexia",
  "definition": "Surface dyslexia is a reading difficulty in which a person has trouble reading aloud words whose spellings do not follow usual sound rules, especially exception words. In the packet, it is described as a reading impairment that can appear in semantic dementia and is linked to reduced support from meaning-based processing for such words.",
